---
description: ssERP project rules (read AGENTS.md for the full guide)
alwaysApply: true
---

Follow `AGENTS.md` in the repository root. Essentials:

- Stack: Next.js 16 App Router, TypeScript strict, Drizzle ORM, PostgreSQL (Neon recommended), npm.
- Scope every business query by the session `companyId` (+ branch via `src/server/branch.ts`); never trust client ids.
- Call `authorize(...)` first in every server action/route handler (`guarded()` / `guardedBranch()`).
- No floating-point money: use `src/server/money.ts`, integer minor units, `numeric(14,2)`, server-computed totals.
- Change unit status only through `src/server/serials.ts`; respect the lock order documented in AGENTS.md.
- Migrations are append-only (`npm run db:generate`, commit the new SQL file).
- Never log raw caught errors (`safeLog`/`safeErrorInfo`), never expose secrets, hashes or cost data without permission.
- New logic needs tests (`*.test.ts`, and `*.db.test.ts` for DB/locking/money/serial changes). Before finishing: `npm run lint && npx tsc --noEmit && npm test`.
